CCTPBridgeModuleIntegration
├── full lifecycle
│   ├── it should bridge USDC end-to-end via PaymentRails → Module → TokenMessenger
│   ├── it should emit ActionExecuted from PaymentRails
│   ├── it should emit BridgeInitiated from Module
│   ├── it should consume all approvals (paymentRails→module, module→messenger)
│   └── it should allow any address to execute (permissionless)
├── tokenMessenger revert
│   ├── it should return false from PaymentRails.executeAction
│   └── it should revoke PaymentRails→Module approval
├── validation failures
│   ├── it should revert when amount is below minBalance
│   ├── it should revert when amount exceeds balance
│   └── it should revert when token is not enabled
├── reconfigure moduleParams
│   └── it should use the new recipient and fee on the next execution
├── consecutive executions
│   └── it should succeed on both and drain the paymentRails
├── preview execution
│   └── it should return (amount - maxFee, usdc)
├── hook data
│   └── it should call depositForBurnWithHook with hookData
├── multi-paymentRails — shared module, independent routing
│   ├── it should bridge from two paymentRails with different recipients via one module
│   ├── it should route to different domains per paymentRails
│   └── it should handle interleaved executions from multiple paymentRails
├── multi-domain — paymentRails reconfiguration
│   └── it should bridge to domain A then reconfigure and bridge to domain B
└── paymentRails reconfiguration
    ├── it should work after disable then re-enable
    └── it should work after swapping to a new module
